WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.401
The Constitution abolished untouchability.

2
00:00:03.401 --> 00:00:05.065
Ending it in practice took

3
00:00:05.065 --> 00:00:05.950
more.

4
00:00:06.275 --> 00:00:10.451
Article 17 abolished untouchability in

5
00:00:10.451 --> 00:00:12.743
1950. A law to punish

6
00:00:12.743 --> 00:00:15.013
it followed in 1955.

7
00:00:15.013 --> 00:00:16.547
In October 1956,

8
00:00:16.547 --> 00:00:19.193
Ambedkar and lakhs of followers

9
00:00:19.193 --> 00:00:22.048
embraced Buddhism at Nagpur.

10
00:00:22.394 --> 00:00:25.558
The 1955 Act was renamed

11
00:00:25.558 --> 00:00:28.407
the Protection of Civil Rights

12
00:00:28.407 --> 00:00:30.118
Act in 1976.

13
00:00:30.805 --> 00:00:33.735
The topic also covers reservations,

14
00:00:33.735 --> 00:00:36.906
and ethnic movements after independence.

15
00:00:37.273 --> 00:00:38.450
Your turn.

16
00:00:38.450 --> 00:00:40.141
Which Article?
